      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we need to convert $P$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 & 2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -2 & 3 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\quad {R}_{4} :={R}_{4}+(1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 & 2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $P$ has $3$ pivots, and therefore the number of pivot columns is $3.$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
